1)Constrains:-In SQL,Constraints are the rules or restrictions/conditions applied on
              a particular table or a column that restricts the type of data that can be
              inserted,deleted or updated
2)Types of constraints are given below
    1)AUTO_INCREMENT:-Automatically generates a unique number for each row
    2)Primary Key:-Uniquely identifies each row in a table
                   Note that primary key cannot be NULL.
